# Quality gates

- Shared entrypoint: `make check` (sectioned fail-fast). Same path as git `pre-push`.
- While building: re-run failing sections or `make check` until green before push.
- Ship: `git push` runs Maximal suite once via pre-push. Do not re-run a full suite solely because you are about to push.
- Never use `git commit --no-verify` or `git push --no-verify`.
- Before `gh pr create`: merge or rebase `origin/main` so HEAD contains main and is conflict-free. Cursor hook `require-pr-up-to-date` enforces this locally for agents. GitHub ruleset does **not** require up-to-date-at-merge.
- New task / worktree: start from latest main (`make sync-main`, then branch). Hook `require-fresh-main-before-branch` blocks new branches/worktrees unless HEAD already contains `origin/main`.
- Setup: `make install` (deps + `pre-commit`/`pre-push` hooks).
- Format: `make fmt` or rely on pre-commit; no ad-hoc formatter bypass.
- Live Gemini scripts live under `backend/scripts/` — manual only, not in `make check`.
- Commands map: see `CLAUDE.md` and the root `Makefile`.
